### Part 1: Java `String` Class (Immutable)
- **Definition:** A sequence of characters. Strings are **objects** in Java.
- **Immutability:** Once created, a String **cannot be changed**. Any operation (like `replace` or `toUpperCase`) creates a **new String** object.
- **String Pool:** Java stores literal strings (`"Hello"`) in a special heap area called the *String Pool*. If you create the same literal twice, Java reuses the existing object from the pool to save memory.
- **Thread-Safety:** Because they are immutable, Strings are automatically safe to use in multi-threaded environments.

#### Common String Methods (Quick Reference)

| Category | Method | Description | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Inspection** | `length()` | Returns number of characters. | `"Java".length()` → `4` |
| | `charAt(index)` | Returns character at specific index. | `"Java".charAt(2)` → `'v'` |
| | `substring(start, end)` | Extracts part of the string (end exclusive). | `"Hello".substring(0,2)` → `"He"` |
| **Search** | `contains(s)` | Checks if substring exists (returns `boolean`). | `"Hello".contains("ell")` → `true` |
| | `indexOf(s)` | Returns first index of substring/char, or `-1`. | `"Hello".indexOf('o')` → `4` |
| | `lastIndexOf(s)` | Returns last index of substring/char. | `"Hello o".lastIndexOf('o')` → `6` |
| **Comparison** | `equals(s)` | Case-**sensitive** comparison. | `"Hi".equals("hi")` → `false` |
| | `equalsIgnoreCase(s)` | **Ignores case** (The method you asked about earlier!). | `"Hi".equalsIgnoreCase("HI")` → `true` |
| | `startsWith(prefix)` | Checks prefix. | `"Java".startsWith("Ja")` → `true` |
| | `endsWith(suffix)` | Checks suffix. | `"Java".endsWith("va")` → `true` |
| **Modification**<br>*(Returns new String)* | `replace(old, new)` | Replaces all occurrences of a char. | `"Java".replace('a','b')` → `"Jbvb"` |
| | `toUpperCase()` | Converts to uppercase. | `"java".toUpperCase()` → `"JAVA"` |
| | `toLowerCase()` | Converts to lowercase. | `"JAVA".toLowerCase()` → `"java"` |
| | `trim()` | Removes leading/trailing whitespace. | `"  Hi  ".trim()` → `"Hi"` |
| | `split(regex)` | Splits into a `String[]` array. | `"a,b,c".split(",")` → `["a","b","c"]` |
| **Conversion** | `toCharArray()` | Converts String to `char[]`. | `"Hi".toCharArray()` → `['H','i']` |

